{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Therefore they shall not eat, etc.</b> The meaning: because the sinew was dislodged from the source of holiness and the kelipah gained dominion over it — this is its nature wherever it becomes impure — and the Creator forbade it, for He is the One who knows. And you will find a sod in this, for this sinew has no taste, and it is a sign of the aspect of the kelipah, which has no taste since holiness was uprooted from it. And there is also a plain sense to say here, but the essential meaning is as I have written."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:41.304134290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}